Description: PlatformPlugin: Add the depth environment; read the user's limits on Plasma
 .
 A platform now says what an output may show in depth: the user's limits
 (depthLimits), whether a window's elements may be shown in depth now
 (depthEnabled: the window is on a stereo output and awake, not lying flat
 behind the active one) and which of its edges lie on the output's edge.
 The defaults give no depth anywhere, so every platform draws exactly what
 it drew before.
 .
 The Plasma platform reads the limits from Stereo KWin's own settings, the
 SunkLimit and PoppedLimit keys of kwinrc's StereoDepth group that System
 Settings' 3D Depth page writes, with KWin's defaults of 10 and 4 pixels of
 a view 1920 wide, and follows their changes. Whether a window is awake
 comes from the compositor; until it can say so, no window shows depth.
